Below are the questions, the quick method to find each answer in Autopsy, and the correct answers.

Q1. What is the MD5 hash of the E01 image?

How to find it: In the left panel click Data Sources → select HASAN2.E01 from the center listing → open File Metadata. The file metadata includes common file info, including hashes.
Answer: 3f08c518adb3b5c1359849657a9b2079

Q2. What is the computer account name?

How to find it: Left panel → Operating System Information → in the center listing pick the Source File that shows full info (the SYSTEM hive). Look at the Name column — that’s the computer account name.
Answer: DESKTOP-0R59DJ3

Q3. List all the user accounts (alphabetical order)

How to find it: Open Operating System User Account. There are many records — the username column can be confusing. Instead, use the Path column to find entries like C:\Users\<username>. Sort the Path column ascending to see the correct user directories.
Answer: H4S4N, joshwa, keshav, sandhya, shreya, sivapriya, srini, suba

Q4. Who was the last user to log into the computer?

How to find it: In the same user-account menu, sort Date Accessed in descending order — the top entry in the Path column shows the last user.
Answer: sivapriya

Q5. What was the IP address of the computer?

How to find it: From Operating System Information look at the Source File Path pointing to vol_vol3. Or navigate: Data Sources → HASAN2.E01 → vol3 → Program Files (x86) → Look@LAN → open irunin.ini and look for the string LANIP.
Answer: 192.168.130.216

Q6. What was the MAC address of the computer? (XX-XX-XX-XX-XX-XX)

How to find it: In the same irunin.ini file look for the string LANNIC that contains the MAC address.
Answer: 08-00-27-2c-c4-b9

Q7. What is the name of the network card on this computer?

How to find it: Go to Operating System Information → click SOFTWARE hive. The Source File Path is /img_HASAN2.E01/vol_vol3/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE. In Autopsy: Data Sources → HASAN2.E01 → vol3 → Windows → System32 → config → open SOFTWARE. In the application subkeys, navigate: Microsoft → Windows NT → CurrentVersion → NetworkCards → 2 → Description.

Note: If you can’t open the application subkey listing, try resetting the VM or re-opening the case.
Answer: Intel(R) PRO/1000 MT Desktop Adapter

Q8. What is the name of the network monitoring tool?

How to find it: Open Installed Programs in the left panel and read the program list — spot the suspicious network-related tool.
Answer: Look@LAN

